{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave","id":939230,"title":"Ride the Wave","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-28T17:42:25-07:00","id":939230,"title":"Ride the Wave","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> <br /> <br /> Riding the Wave:<br /> <br /> \u200bSeems this is a bit of a contentious topic on how it works. Does this invoke frenzy or does it require you to be already starting to frenzy?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T18:38:16-07:00","id":939254,"title":"","content":"Well, it could be used to voluntarily initiate Frenzy in 1e. In fact, that was literally the entire purpose of Riding the Wave in 1e. So, there's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T18:45:18-07:00","id":939258,"title":"","content":"By the way, quite everything could provoke the frenzy, with different modificators: insults, injuries, property damage, hungry etc.<br /> You just need to not resist with the roll.<br /> Anyway I rule that you can volountary ride the wave at will: the Beast is something that always want to take control; the citated factors just give her an hook to submit the vampire will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T19:23:00-07:00","id":939283,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty/page3\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-majesty/page3</a><br /> <br /> That thread already has some really great points. I agree with Mania and Elderand, that you have to be provoked. Once provoked you may roll and spend the WP to try to ride the wave. Mania has some really valid points with direct quotes from the book.<br /> <br /> Also If you want to set a baseline where every insult sends your vampire into a frenzy. that would be a short violent game. Because it shouldn't be insults that you want, but even insults where say the Prince insulted you. Or the Primogen or some place you dont want it to happen.<br /> <br /> It seems some people think you can Ride the wave whenever you want, and some people think you need to be provoked. Which is why I think the question was directed at Rose to clarify as it never was in that last thread.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=816156#post816156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">To ride the wave, spend a Willpower point, and make the<br /> normal Resolve + Composure resistance roll. The Willpower<br /> point does not add to this roll.<b> Success holds off the frenzy for<br /> a turn</b> as if she\u2019d spent Willpower to fight the frenzy. She can<br /> continue to do this until she fails, runs out of Willpower, or<br /> until she accumulates five successes. Treat any failure on this<br /> roll as a dramatic failure.</span></i></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=816156#post816156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are you holding off Frenzy for a turn if there's nothing to hold off yet?<br /> <br /> You resist or you Ride or you give in, in response to a Frenzy trigger.<br /> <br /> If you can just Ride whenever, there's no point to Coil of the Wyrm's &quot;enter Frenzy whenever you want&quot; Coils. It's heavily implied if not directly stated.<br /> <br /> Also see the following:</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=816156#post816156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">However, you may choose the Beast\u2019s desire and specific target<br /> at the outset. <b>This desire does not have to align with the<br /> provocation.</b> For example, if Victoria risks frenzy because she\u2019s<br /> starved, she might choose to kill Dominic instead of feeding.</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> There has to be provocation. Just like normal Frenzy.<br /> <br /> It's also called &quot;riding the wave of frenzy.&quot; How can you ride a wave that doesn't exist?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=816156#post816156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the Coils of the Wyrm:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">When<br /> he enters frenzy the Dragon may opt to forego all resistance,<br /> falling into a state that will not cease until the Beast is sated<br /> <b>(though he may still ride the wave)</b>.</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> When a vampire enters Frenzy with this Coil, he can't resist, but he can <b>still</b> Ride the Wave. Still. As in, that's a standard potential response to Frenzy. Not something granted by the Coil.<br /> <br /> You may not find the evidence sufficient, you may not like that this interpretation weakens your Frenzy build or whatever, but saying there is no evidence to support this interpretation is patently false.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 07-28-2016, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T19:39:03-07:00","id":939290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939283#post939283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty/page3\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-majesty/page3</a><br /> <br /> That thread already has some really great points. I agree with Mania and Elderand, that you have to be provoked. Once provoked you may roll and spend the WP to try to ride the wave. Mania has some really valid points with direct quotes from the book.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm pretty sure reading that thread was what prompted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar460_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"460\" data-vbnamecard=\"460\">Rani Neferet</a> to start this one, rather than necro that one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939283#post939283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also If you want to set a baseline where every insult sends your vampire into a frenzy. that would be a short violent game. Because it shouldn't be insults that you want, but even insults where say the Prince insulted you. Or the Primogen or some place you dont want it to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I fully agree with you there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939283#post939283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems some people think you can Ride the wave whenever you want, and some people think you need to be provoked. Which is why I think the question was directed at Rose to clarify as it never was in that last thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhmm. To be honest, I think people are a little spoiled by the developers being so active on these forums. Like, getting word of god on an issue is nice, but I really don't think it should be expected. Just my personal opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939283#post939283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">: <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">To ride the wave, spend a Willpower point, and make the<br /> normal Resolve + Composure resistance roll. The Willpower<br /> point does not add to this roll.<b> Success holds off the frenzy for<br /> a turn</b> as if she\u2019d spent Willpower to fight the frenzy. She can<br /> continue to do this until she fails, runs out of Willpower, or<br /> until she accumulates five successes. Treat any failure on this<br /> roll as a dramatic failure.</span></i></span><br /> <br /> How are you holding off Frenzy for a turn if there's nothing to hold off yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're holding off the Frenzy that you triggered by spending the Willpower. The one that you fall into if you don't succeed your rolls to Ride the Wave.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939283#post939283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You resist or you Ride or you give in, in response to a Frenzy trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is also possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939283#post939283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can just Ride whenever, there's no point to Coil of the Wyrm's &quot;enter Frenzy whenever you want&quot; Coils. It's heavily implied if not directly stated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also pointed out in that thread, Wyrm 1 allows you to enter a directed Frenzy without having to roll, without risk of falling into an undirected Frenzy, and without having to spend multiple turns trying to achieve controlled Frenzy. Under either interpretation, it is strictly better than Riding the Wave.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939283#post939283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also see the following:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">However, you may choose the Beast\u2019s desire and specific target<br /> at the outset. <b>This desire does not have to align with the<br /> provocation.</b> For example, if Victoria risks frenzy because she\u2019s<br /> starved, she might choose to kill Dominic instead of feeding.</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> There has to be provocation. Just like normal Frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You supply the provocation by spending a point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939283#post939283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also called &quot;riding the wave of frenzy.&quot; How can you ride a wave that doesn't exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it does exist. It's the thing you fall into if you fail the roll to Ride the Wave.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939283#post939283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the Coils of the Wyrm:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">When<br /> he enters frenzy the Dragon may opt to forego all resistance,<br /> falling into a state that will not cease until the Beast is sated<br /> <b>(though he may still ride the wave)</b>.</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> When a vampire enters Frenzy with this Coil, he can't resist, but he can <b>still</b> Ride the Wave. Still. As in, that's a standard potential response to Frenzy. Not something granted by the Coil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Yes it is. This doesn't in any way imply that it can't be done voluntarily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939283#post939283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may not find the evidence sufficient, you may not like that this interpretation weakens your Frenzy build or whatever, but saying there is no evidence to support this interpretation is patently false.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say there is no evidence to support that interpretation. Only that the evidence in support of it is flimsy, and inconsistent with the way Riding the Wave worked in 1e and the way it is presented in the fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-28-2016, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T19:55:53-07:00","id":939296,"title":"","content":"Hmm.. my quotes for some reason.. did not quote properly.. &gt;.&gt; bah! I dont know what I did wrong. That stuff was All Mania which someone ( might have been you, responded to ) I was just saying I agreed with Mania's logic. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T20:12:34-07:00","id":939305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939296#post939296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.. my quotes for some reason.. did not quote properly.. &gt;.&gt; bah! I dont know what I did wrong. That stuff was All Mania which someone ( might have been you, responded to ) I was just saying I agreed with Mania's logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly stayed out of that discussion at the time, though I read it all and popped in to point out that Wyrm 1 is better than Riding the Wave under either interpretation. I think the text could be interpreted either way, but based on the way it worked in 1e and the way it's portrayed in the fiction, I believe the intent is for Riding the Wave to be possible to initiate voluntarily without any other trigger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T21:12:33-07:00","id":939323,"title":"","content":"I'm on the side that says that, in pretty much any situation you'd want to Ride the Wave, there's a corresponding element that can be seen as a provocation. Put the egg before the chicken!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T22:25:59-07:00","id":939352,"title":"","content":"Why exactly would we use &quot;It's not like 1e&quot; as a reason to dismiss all the aforementioned evidence?<br /> <br /> Plenty of 2e doesn't work like 1e. That's a plus in most cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T04:33:55-07:00","id":939442,"title":"","content":"Toolkit. Use whichever interpretation fits your game/table better.<br /> <br /> For me a provocation is needed first, not created out of nothing. A wave is coming (provocation) - I can let it wash over me, losing myself to the tide and its direction. I can try and withstand it, hoping I'm still upright and in the same place after it hits. Or I can try and ride it, using its power and fury but in a direction more of my choosing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T04:41:28-07:00","id":939449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939442#post939442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me a provocation is needed first, not created out of nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you use a memory as the provocation, even if the circumstances around you presently wouldn't provoke you to frenzy?<br /> <br /> And remember, if you want to constantly 'ride the wave' you can <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZXnaJDf-gERGZe97JoIqj2bffJyrjal8Ch4xWD4L9lg/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">pledge yourself to Belial</a> and become the coolest of vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-29-2016, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T05:57:36-07:00","id":939475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939449#post939449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use a memory as the provocation, even if the circumstances around you presently wouldn't provoke you to frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, I'd want some active actions to be in play for some kind of self-provocation. Causing pain to yourself. Pounding the chest, yelling, trying to get furious. Smearing vitae over your hands or face while hungry so you can smell it. Something more than just a turn and a willpower.<br /> <br /> If it was a particularly dramatic memory, I might let that fly once or twice but it would have to be recently fresh - AND - if the player is willing to say this particular memory is a provocation on its own, I would reserve the right to use that memory myself during a dramatic scene when the player wasn't expecting it.<br /> <br /> But I probably wouldn't allow a single memory to be used over and over again for a self-provocation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T06:31:59-07:00","id":939491,"title":"","content":"Can I ask this? Is there a situation where you'd want to ride the wave, and you don't already have some provocation? The list of triggers for frenzy are not all-inclusive in the first place. Furthermore, there are plenty of situations where you could be provoked, but the story calls for no frenzies, so the rolls are ignored.<br /> <br /> Frenzy is a dramatic tool. So, if we have a situation where its appropriate to Ride the Wave, wouldn't it be a dramatic situation for a regular frenzy as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T07:11:59-07:00","id":939506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939352#post939352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why exactly would we use &amp;quot;It's not like 1e&amp;quot; as a reason to dismiss all the aforementioned evidence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I don't find the afformentioned evidence particularly compelling. I gave my counter-arguments and I've yet to see any rebuttal.<br /> <br /> Also, you seem to be ignoring the &quot;how it's used in the fiction&quot; part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T07:18:55-07:00","id":939510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939491#post939491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I ask this? Is there a situation where you'd want to ride the wave, and you don't already have some provocation? The list of triggers for frenzy are not all-inclusive in the first place. Furthermore, there are plenty of situations where you could be provoked, but the story calls for no frenzies, so the rolls are ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on your threshold between general tension and frenzy provocation. Setting up an ambush, sabotaging a location, escaping from a prison, during a race or contest - those could all be tense situations, but not necessarily situations that would provoke a frenzy. I would at least feel reluctant to call for a frenzy check just based on the tension (unless it really worked with the story). However, the mechanical bonuses still might be useful in those scenes. But I suspect those cases will be outliers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Frenzy is a dramatic tool. So, if we have a situation where its appropriate to Ride the Wave, wouldn't it be a dramatic situation for a regular frenzy as well? </div> </div> </div>I think that's probably 90% of the cases, yeah. My only quibble is that I'd say the player should be allowed <i>some </i>leeway for when frenzy is dramatically appropriate or when their character feels provoked. Assuming they weren't abusing the situation, I'd let it fly even if I just thought the scene was tense and hadn't called for a check yet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T07:35:04-07:00","id":939523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939352#post939352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why exactly would we use &quot;It's not like 1e&quot; as a reason to dismiss all the aforementioned evidence?<br /> <br /> Plenty of 2e doesn't work like 1e. That's a plus in most cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>First edition is ok as a last resort, but, I agree, That we really shouldnt use first edition because sooooo much has been changed. There are a lot of similarities, but nearly every discipline and hell even frenzy changed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939491#post939491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I ask this? Is there a situation where you'd want to ride the wave, and you don't already have some provocation? The list of triggers for frenzy are not all-inclusive in the first place. Furthermore, there are plenty of situations where you could be provoked, but the story calls for no frenzies, so the rolls are ignored.<br /> <br /> Frenzy is a dramatic tool. So, if we have a situation where its appropriate to Ride the Wave, wouldn't it be a dramatic situation for a regular frenzy as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>What if you just walked into a &lt;place&gt; to be a jerk and wanted to hurt as many people as possible before hand, you know you can do it better in a death frenzy.... simply wanted to, picked the place out of a phone book..<br /> <br /> It goes back to that baseline again.. do you want your vampire to frenzy every time someone calls him a jerk for flips him the bird, every time he remembers that one shitty day?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939475#post939475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, I'd want some active actions to be in play for some kind of self-provocation. Causing pain to yourself. Pounding the chest, yelling, trying to get furious. Smearing vitae over your hands or face while hungry so you can smell it. Something more than just a turn and a willpower.<br /> <br /> If it was a particularly dramatic memory, I might let that fly once or twice but it would have to be recently fresh - AND - if the player is willing to say this particular memory is a provocation on its own, I would reserve the right to use that memory myself during a dramatic scene when the player wasn't expecting it.<br /> <br /> But I probably wouldn't allow a single memory to be used over and over again for a self-provocation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that I would not let a memory work. You would desensitize yourself to it eventually.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939506#post939506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I don't find the afformentioned evidence particularly compelling. I gave my counter-arguments and I've yet to see any rebuttal.<br /> <br /> Also, you seem to be ignoring the &quot;how it's used in the fiction&quot; part.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see rebuttal. I see valid points. Perhaps is that because we are seeing what we want to see? I am not entirely sure. Also Vampires sparkle and can walk in the sun in fiction...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for more &quot;Evidence&quot; If you can ride the wave in an Unprovoked frenzy .. What does this coil of the dragon mean? Literally if EVERYONE can do it unprompted, why would anyone take this? <br /> <br /> &quot;Stir the Beast \u2022<br /> Before the Beast can be tamed a Dragon must first know<br /> how to wake it. For a point of Willpower he may enter frenzy<br /> unprompted. &quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 07-29-2016, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T07:54:05-07:00","id":939534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939523#post939523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if you just walked into a &lt;place&gt; to be a jerk and wanted to hurt as many people as possible before hand, you know you can do it better in a death frenzy.... simply wanted to, picked the place out of a phone book..<br /> <br /> It goes back to that baseline again.. do you want your vampire to frenzy every time someone calls him a jerk for flips him the bird, every time he remembers that one shitty day?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think 'opening a jar,' would be a better example. Honestly I was having fun dwelling on it and I was thinking about a Blood Potency 10 vampire with 8 Resolve and 9 Composure but 1 Strength, who's going to struggle to open a jar in front of this girl they like, but decides to use Ride the Wave to get the strength required to open it. There was also a similar vampire who was at a gym with his friends, who bet him he couldn't press 500 lbs.<br /> <br /> Basically if you can activate Ride the Wave whenever you want, and you can choose the end goal of your Frenzy, you can now choose short term goals that require Strength, Stamina and Dexterity. Once you get over 2 Blood Potency you're just spending 1 Willpower a turn for however many extra dice you get rather than 1 Vitae for 2 from Physical Intensity. Once you're over 3, you can eschew Willpower's +3. Obviously if you really need, you can then spend Vitae in addition to your Riding.<br /> <br /> This is the type of fear that spawns a lot of 'is the rule really like that?' questions.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It's been a while. If you look into it, Riding the Wave is fairly complicated, it reminds me of diablerie mechanically. Actually using it as a Strength or other Physical Attribute substitute would require a lot of Willpower, unless one had a lot of Resolve or Composure. Basically really amping yourself up for something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-29-2016, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T08:04:10-07:00","id":939538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939523#post939523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for more &quot;Evidence&quot; If you can ride the wave in an Unprovoked frenzy .. What does this coil of the dragon mean? Literally if EVERYONE can do it unprompted, why would anyone take this?<br /> <br /> &quot;Stir the Beast \u2022<br /> Before the Beast can be tamed a Dragon must first know<br /> how to wake it. For a point of Willpower he may enter frenzy<br /> unprompted. &quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree personally with your overall interpretation on provocation, <b>Stir the Beast</b> is also a Reflexive action allowing you to pre-empt a normal frenzy with your own (different) frenzy-goal for 1 WP. That's still an advantage regardless of the provocation debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T08:10:24-07:00","id":939540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939523#post939523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see rebuttal.</div> </div> </div> </div>To my counter-arguments to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a>'s citations of supporting evidence for their position? Could you quote them because I literally do not see it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939384#post939384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see valid points.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do too, I just haven't been convinced by them and have given my reasons for not in my responses to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a>'s points that you quoted upthread. Those points have not been addressed as far as I can see. Which, don't get me wrong, no one is obligated to respond to. If your interpretation works for your group, that's cool. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939384#post939384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Vampires sparkle and can walk in the sun in fiction...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in official Requiem Fiction, which is the fiction I was referring to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939384#post939384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for more &quot;Evidence&quot; If you can ride the wave in an Unprovoked frenzy .. What does this coil of the dragon mean? Literally if EVERYONE can do it unprompted, why would anyone take this? <br /> <br /> &quot;Stir the Beast \u2022<br /> Before the Beast can be tamed a Dragon must first know<br /> how to wake it. For a point of Willpower he may enter frenzy<br /> unprompted. &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I have addressed this like three times and no one has acknowledged it yet. Stir the Beast doesn't require a roll, doesn't require multiple turns to do, and has no risk of failing and leaving you in an uncontrolled Frenzy, which makes it a straight upgrade over Riding the Wave under either interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-29-2016, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T09:08:17-07:00","id":939573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939540#post939540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have addressed this like three times and no one has acknowledged it yet. Stir the Beast doesn't require a roll, doesn't require multiple turns to do, and has no risk of failing and leaving you in an uncontrolled Frenzy, which makes it a straight upgrade over Riding the Wave under either interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two people look at the same photograph and see two different things. People read the same book and gather different information. People innately interpret things differently.<br /> <br /> <i>Stir the Beast \u2022<br /> Before the Beast can be tamed a Dragon must first know<br /> how to wake it. For a point of Willpower he may enter frenzy<br /> unprompted. </i><br /> <br /> My interpretation: You have to be taught ( the way the Ordo only teaches ) to learn how to go into a frenzy unprovoked. You have to learn/know how to &quot;wake it&quot; wake the beast. Once you have learned how to do that you can do all of the following:<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>When he does so the Dragon selects a target or goal,<br /> no more than a few words, which becomes the objective of his<br /> frenzy. </i><br /> <br /> Once he has frenzied and picked his target. The following is clarified:<br /> <br /> <i>He has no more control over his actions than he would<br /> in an involuntary frenzy (p. 103), and all rolls to escape frenzy<br /> before the stated objective is met are made at a \u20132 die penalty.<br /> When the original goal is no longer pressing or possible, the<br /> frenzy ends.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Additional mechanics needed, we needed to know how fast this was and if we can do it when provoked as well.<br /> <br /> Using Stir the Beast is a reflexive action, and it can be used<br /> to avoid involuntary frenzy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Normal riding the wave: Has been broken down already and I dont want to repeat it All, but there are implied words there but here is my evidence to support the text:<br /> <br /> Will power <b>and </b>Normal rolls. Normal roll comes from being provoked. Hold off the frenzy for a turn.. Cant hold off something that's not there.<br /> Once you succeed you can choose your objective and that doesnt have to align with the original provocation. If there was no original provocation, then that cant hold true.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again: I totally understand that this is an upgrade to normal riding the wave which could take many turns. But I cant ignore all the implications and I understand that's just me. You have to learn it. But I dont think the Intent was to just make riding the wave faster. I think it was to offer something that wasnt available to ALL vampires. As the coils should be. They should be something that is not available to other vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> At this point I think Rose is the only one who could change my mind. I am not infallible, so I could be totally wrong. And I am ok with that. you might called me spoiled. but I do not EXPECT it. I just hope that she can settle the debate and I think it is super awesome of her that she does this. That she comes and clarifies stuff. But I dont expect it, just hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 07-29-2016, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T10:27:33-07:00","id":939621,"title":"","content":"Resisting frenzy is also a reflexive action, not extended. You can roll at the same turn of provocation or you can opt to spend willpower to delay that roll, turning it into riding the wave which is an extended action and increase your odds of success, but you are NOT required to do so. The coil simply turns an extended action into a reflexive one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T10:46:35-07:00","id":939636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939573#post939573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again: I totally understand that this is an upgrade to normal riding the wave which could take many turns. But I cant ignore all the implications and I understand that's just me. You have to learn it. But I dont think the Intent was to just make riding the wave faster. I think it was to offer something that wasnt available to ALL vampires. As the coils should be. They should be something that is not available to other vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair and in my opinion a totally reasonable interpretation of the text. I personally don't agree with it, and I don't think at-will Riding the Wave invalidates the Coil's usefulness, which is what it seemed to me like folks were trying to argue by citing the Coil as evidence against at-will Frenzy. But if what you meant was that the way it's written makes it seem like &quot;entering Frenzy unprovoked&quot; is a new thing the Coil allows you to do rather than an upgrade to something you could already do, that makes sense.<br /> <br /> As a slightly off-topic aside, I don't agree that all coils should grant new powers, and in fact my interpretation is that the point of the Coils of the Dragon is to improve upon inherent qualities of the template, or to mitigate inherent weaknesses of the template. Entirely new powers is the purview of Scales. I wonder if this discrepancy in our conceptualizations of the Coils was playing into our recent disagreement re: the utility of Voivode 3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939573#post939573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point I think Rose is the only one who could change my mind. I am not infallible, so I could be totally wrong. And I am ok with that. you might called me spoiled. but I do not EXPECT it. I just hope that she can settle the debate and I think it is super awesome of her that she does this. That she comes and clarifies stuff. But I dont expect it, just hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I did not mean to call you spoiled. I agree that it would be nice to have clarification from Rose if she has the time and inclination, and don't fault people for seeking out her input. I've just been irritated by the recent trend of folks tagging her into discussions as if to settle arguments, instead of discussing how different people interpret the rules and why and using their own best judgment for the needs of their own games. That mini-rant of mine was an inappropriate way for me to express that frustration, and I apologize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-29-2016, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T10:47:41-07:00","id":939637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939621#post939621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resisting frenzy is also a reflexive action, not extended. You can roll at the same turn of provocation or you can opt to spend willpower to delay that roll, turning it into riding the wave which is an extended action and increase your odds of success, but you are NOT required to do so. The coil simply turns an extended action into a reflexive one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also removes the need to roll and the risk of failing the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T11:18:33-07:00","id":939660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939636#post939636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a slightly off-topic aside, I don't agree that all coils should grant new powers, and in fact my interpretation is that the point of the Coils of the Dragon is to improve upon inherent qualities of the template, or to mitigate inherent weaknesses of the template. Entirely new powers is the purview of Scales. I wonder if this discrepancy in our conceptualizations of the Coils was playing into our recent disagreement re: the utility or Ascendant 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasnt really saying &quot;new powers&quot; but things that not all vampires can do. And yes I believe this ties into that. While every vampire can blood bond, it is clear now that not every vampire, only dragons, can do it in one scene. While every vampire's vitae is addicting, only dragons can make vampire specific addiction. While every vampire can frenzy and ride the wave. I do not believe every vampire can do it without being provoked (and the coil gives them that and upgrades it by removing failure) We agree that they make things better. ( and I believe ) while still offering up something that not all vampires can do. <br /> I think of it like disciplines, and they are disciplines, But each discipline offers a vampire a unique and better thing. While every vampire can charm someone through persuasion. not every vampire can &quot;<i>Charm</i>&quot; someone<br /> While every vampire can scare the crap out of someone, not every vampire can make someone see or hear things that aren't there. <br /> <br /> That's kind of my logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T11:28:12-07:00","id":939667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939637#post939637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also removes the need to roll and the risk of failing the roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I fullz agree with this statement. No matter the intention behind Riding the Wave, Wyrm 1 always grants access to a strictly better frenzy mechanics.<br /> <br /> Also, while i personally understand the intention behind the rules to be that Kindred can attempt to ride without any prior triggers, I cannot imagine that situations, in which characters would want to ride without there being some dramatic reason present in the first place, would be very common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T11:28:17-07:00","id":939669,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939510#post939510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on your threshold between general tension and frenzy provocation.</div> </div> </div> </div> Considering that &quot;expecting provocation&quot; is itself listed as a provocation for a frenzy check? That's some very broad situations where general tension and frenzy provocation are aligned. I can't really see it being that different, personally.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What if you just walked into a &lt;place&gt; to be a jerk and wanted to hurt as many people as possible before hand, you know you can do it better in a death frenzy.... simply wanted to, picked the place out of a phone book..</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> First of all, are you a psychopath for that? Going in a place and unleashing the Beast is pretty self destructive and unrealistic character.<br /> <br /> Secondly, if you're causing a frenzy scene with all that death and blood, your'e Beast is going to be provoked. &quot;Seeing a trivial wound&quot; and &quot;expecting provocation&quot; are both there, so.. yeah, provocation for frenzy, achieved.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It goes back to that baseline again.. do you want your vampire to frenzy every time someone calls him a jerk for flips him the bird, every time he remembers that one shitty day? </div> </div> </div> To be blunt? Insults by a superior or inferior are frenzy provocations. Just because the ST chooses to not call for a roll does not mean its not a provocation, and I feel that an ST opting to not call for a check for story reasons should not be used as an reason to disallow Riding the Wave. Because that's what the argument feels like here. &quot;The ST didn't call for a check, therefore you cannot Ride.&quot; </span></span></span><br /> <br /> Also, as an aside, I really don't understand the whole &quot;but it ruins a Coil!!!&quot; as an argument. For all we know, there could have been any number of reasons for the Coil to be worded the way it was, including simply falling behind edits, misreading, or general misunderstandings of the larger rules and how they interact. I just find it a very unconvincing argument. Personally, I've used that Coil to pseudo-escape from the Mesmerized Condition, which alone is worth its XP cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-29-2016, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T11:41:25-07:00","id":939680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939669#post939669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that &quot;expecting provocation&quot; is itself listed as a provocation for a frenzy check? That's some very broad situations where general tension and frenzy provocation are aligned. I can't really see it being that different, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's listed as an influence that modifies frenzy, not as a provocation <b>of </b>frenzy. The chart does mention, &quot;<i>Under the right circumstances, any of these things could be a provocation to frenzy.</i>&quot; But that's just a reiteration of the toolkit nature of 2E. Unless you are going to argue 'On Elysium Grounds' is a provocations in and of itself, some are just modifiers to the other provocation. I'd say the same for the '...from your Touchstone' modifier, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">To be blunt? Insults by a superior or inferior are frenzy provocations.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><br /> <br /> Only under the right circumstances. Not automatically every time...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just because the ST chooses to not call for a roll does not mean its not a provocation, and I feel that an ST opting to not call for a check for story reasons should not be used as an reason to disallow Riding the Wave. Because that's what the argument feels like here. &quot;The ST didn't call for a check, therefore you cannot Ride.&quot; </div> </div> </div>100% agree with this.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T11:46:47-07:00","id":939683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939669#post939669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Considering that &quot;expecting provocation&quot; is itself listed as a provocation for a frenzy check? That's some very broad situations where general tension and frenzy provocation are aligned. I can't really see it being that different, personally.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It's listed as provocation or circumstance <b>modifier </b>to the roll for a frenzy. As with the Humanity list, the things on the circumstance list are possibilities not ALWAYSes? is that a word.. i think not. I cant find a better one.. HAHA<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939669#post939669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">First of all, are you a psychopath for that? Going in a place and unleashing the Beast is pretty self destructive and unrealistic character.<br /> <br /> Secondly, if you're causing a frenzy scene with all that death and blood, your'e Beast is going to be provoked. &quot;Seeing a trivial wound&quot; and &quot;expecting provocation&quot; are both there, so.. yeah, provocation for frenzy, achieved.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> psychopath or not is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Causing the scene and walking in that way are two very different things. One Scenario I have already frenzied and killed people. Second scenario I did it without frenzying and therefor now will frenzy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939669#post939669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> To be blunt? Insults by a superior or inferior are frenzy provocations. Just because the ST chooses to not call for a roll does not mean its not a provocation, and I feel that an ST opting to not call for a check for story reasons should not be used as an reason to disallow Riding the Wave. Because that's what the argument feels like here. &quot;The ST didn't call for a check, therefore you cannot Ride.&quot; </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>not at all what I was saying. What I was saying was there needs to be a provocation, not that a story teller called for it or not. If every time the prince calls you a Childe, sends you into a frenzy. then your life is going to be a short one. That is why the story teller's dont call for it, because it's not dramatic anymore. It loses it's meaning if every little thing set you off. I dont want to speak for everyone, but I think?? We all agree that the point of these games is to be dramatic, to have meaning...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939669#post939669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, as an aside, I really don't understand the whole &quot;but it ruins a Coil!!!&quot; as an argument. For all we know, there could have been any number of reasons for the Coil to be worded the way it was, including simply falling behind edits, misreading, or general misunderstandings of the larger rules and how they interact. I just find it a very unconvincing argument. Personally, I've used that Coil to pseudo-escape from the Mesmerized Condition, which alone is worth its XP cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right we dont know what they were thinking and here in lies the interpretation. I could show a picture and we could all interpret the meaning differently. I could show you a short story and we would all walk away with something different. Humans interpret things different. Even if we went to the same concert we would have different experiences... Same with this. We interpret the meaning differently and that's ok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 07-29-2016, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T11:57:18-07:00","id":939687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939660#post939660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasnt really saying &quot;new powers&quot; but things that not all vampires can do. And yes I believe this ties into that. While every vampire can blood bond, it is clear now that not every vampire, only dragons, can do it in one scene. While every vampire's vitae is addicting, only dragons can make vampire specific addiction. While every vampire can frenzy and ride the wave. I do not believe every vampire can do it without being provoked (and the coil gives them that and upgrades it by removing failure) We agree that they make things better. ( and I believe ) while still offering up something that not all vampires can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Poor choice of words on my part, sorry. My interpretation is that Coils don't allow you to do things not every vampire can do, they make you better at things every vampire can do, or circumvent a limitation all vampires have. Every vampire can form a Blood Bond, but Initiates of the Voivode can do it faster. Every vampire can stay awake during the day, but Initiates of the Ascendent can do it without becoming Lethargic or risking falling back asleep. Every vampire can goad themselves into Frenzy, but Initiates of the Wyrm can do it faster, and without having to risk falling into a Frenzy that won't end until they experience a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939660#post939660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think of it like disciplines, and they are disciplines, But each discipline offers a vampire a unique and better thing. While every vampire can charm someone through persuasion. not every vampire can &quot;<i>Charm</i>&quot; someone<br /> While every vampire can scare the crap out of someone, not every vampire can make someone see or hear things that aren't there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coils are not Disciplines though, and one of the key differences between Coils and Disciplines is that Coils are modifications to the template, where Disciplines are powers in their own right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939660#post939660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's kind of my logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I don't think we're likely to come to an agreement on our understandings of the Coils, but I'm cool with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-29-2016, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T12:07:41-07:00","id":939692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939687#post939687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Coils are not Disciplines though, and one of the key differences between Coils and Disciplines is that Coils are modifications to the template, where Disciplines are powers in their own right.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why are they listed in disciplines in 2 different sections of the book? What are they then?<br /> <br /> Quick reference guide on pg 83<br /> Disciplines<br /> Animalism: The ability to communicate with and<br /> command animals. Each character starts with three dots<br /> of Disciplines, at least two of which must be in clan.<br /> Auspex: Forbidden understanding and senses.<br /> Celerity: Impossible speed.<br /> Coils of the Dragon: Secrets that transcend the Curse.<br /> Cr\u00faac: The terrifying rituals of the Circle of the Crone.<br /> Dominate: The ability to control the mind.<br /> Majesty: The power to command trust and adoration.<br /> Nightmare: The power to harness terror.<br /> Obfuscate: Powers of stealth and distraction.<br /> Protean: The power to change shape.<br /> Resilience: Immense toughness.<br /> Theban Sorcery: The dark miracles of the Lancea et<br /> Sanctum.<br /> Vigor: Inhuman strength.<br /> <br /> <br /> and of course in the Discipline chapter and in the Discipline index of that chapter? you can even pick one as your spare dot upon character creation. 2 in clan and 1 out of it.. which could be a coil or sorcery","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T12:11:38-07:00","id":939696,"title":"","content":"Because they are mechanically similar to Disciplines, and where else would you put them? However, according to the section on Coils,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Coils of the Dragon stand as proof that the Order\u2019s methods bring results. Coils, <b>like Disciplines</b>, are on a ladder from one to five dots. With each dot comes a potent and everlasting change to a vampire\u2019s accursed state. </div> </div> </div>The use of the phrase &quot;like Disciplines&quot; implies that they are similar to, but distinct from, Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T18:12:24-07:00","id":939882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939636#post939636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I did not mean to call you spoiled. I agree that it would be nice to have clarification from Rose if she has the time and inclination, and don't fault people for seeking out her input. I've just been irritated by the recent trend of folks tagging her into discussions as if to settle arguments, instead of discussing how different people interpret the rules and why and using their own best judgment for the needs of their own games. That mini-rant of mine was an inappropriate way for me to express that frustration, and I apologize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so you don't feel alone in this sentiment, as a part-time poster but full-time lurker, I agree. Had Rose been the second post, this trend would have been a 'call-and-answer' type of affair. Useful, but not very intriguing. I personally enjoy to reasoned and even pensive debate seen here. I also think it is healthier.<br /> <br /> Of course, if Rose reads this, I don't want her to doubt her role. In fact, if it was up to me to shape our polis, when Rose contributes, it should not end debate. From then on, argument could be of the form 'Yes, author intent was x but y makes so much more sense for z'. So carry on contributing Rose (as if you need my permission or validation) as we shall (if I have my way) only use your input as a ruling in a hurry, but as wise counsel at our leisure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T19:42:52-07:00","id":939910,"title":"","content":"Please don't discourage Rose from commenting on this thread. Also, I think it would be fantastic if the FAQ got updated some with some of her answers that aren't there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T21:10:56-07:00","id":939942,"title":"","content":"As the player of the character and event that sparked this whole discussion I feel it's pertinent to quote this piece right here:<br /> <br /> VTR 2E 91: &quot;Every step she takes, every corner she turns, a Kindred's Beast stands ready to face threats, to defend territory, and most importantly, to feed. To the Beast, everything is a challenge, a potential conquest, a meal, or a combination of the three. To other predators, the Beast is a palpable thing, something that identifies another monster. This presence, the predatory aura, builds a paradox in Kindred society. On one hand, it guarantees vampires will never be civil, as all remain one misstep away from each other's throats. On the other hand, it forces Kindred to hold tight to traditions and propriety, in order to keep the Beast at bay and force a modicum of nicety.&quot;<br /> <br /> Let's not forget what we're playing. monsters, always lurking under the surface, always ready to compete and fight, fuck, feed, or flee. While I agree that calling for a frenzy roll for every particular provocation is hardly good or effective role-play, there is absolutely nothing in the first 2 paragraphs (of Ride the Wave) that requires the player to have a provocation. The rule states a WP must be spent, and dice must be rolled. The question that should be asked is &quot;what modifiers do we place on the roll?&quot; Minor wound? +1. Party members dying?? -1 depending.<br /> <br /> Provocation's mention in paragraph three is a comparative reference to the fact that under normal Frenzy circumstances a character does not choose the target, nor the desire, it is not a statement of requirement to initiate the task.<br /> <br /> The resistance mentioned in paragraph two is both comparative to the fact that it is the same type of roll as a Resistance roll but the second portion clarifies how they function differently. It is also indicative of the fact that from the moment you choose to spend a Willpower point to initiate a Ride the Wave, you WILL frenzy. It becomes a question of what kind of frenzy, not IF you frenzy. Your resistance roll at that point is to see if you can keep ahold of the leash and your footing, after issuing a Kill command.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, I don't need a lesson in the fact that 2E is different than 1E, but 1E DID have NO requirement of provocation to initiate a Ride the Wave, and neither did Dark Ages: Vampire. I can't seem to find it in an edition of VtM that I own, even mentioned as an option, I'm sure it's under Path of the Beast in a splat book I don't feel like digging for.<br /> <br /> Some things do change, and some rolls get modified. But the Beast is still the Beast, and not the Cuddle-Bear.<br /> <br /> And for anyone curious, in the third round, I did lose my shit and resume Normal Frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12019,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","user":"CrimsonOwl","date":". 07-30-2016, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T00:10:43-07:00","id":939983,"title":"","content":"You know how all the <i>cool</i> Vampires Ride the Beast?<br /> <br /> They light a big ol' fire, and play a grand ol' game of Frenzy Chicken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T04:24:45-07:00","id":940043,"title":"","content":"In that case, everything is just a modifer, and there's no guidelines on what counts as a provocation other than what a player or ST says it is. And, if a player has any input at all at what they'd feel provoked about (and they should, given that its their character), then that's the same thing as letting one Ride the Wave, or at least attempt, at any point.<br /> <br /> &quot;Under the right circumstances&quot; in this case means that we have a player justifying their desire to Ride the Wave. If they have a reason to feel provoked enough to make the roll, then they should be allowed to. This isn't about an ST forcing a frenzy check all the time, but when its appropriate for a character to try and Ride the Wave, or the player deliberately asking for a frenzy check due to the character's emotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-30-2016, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T04:42:43-07:00","id":940047,"title":"","content":"I've mostly been trying to stay out of this due to not wanting to rehash an old argument, but this has been bugging me for a while;<br /> <br /> I mentioned something related to the lack of target for you to change when you Ride the Wave without provocation.<br /> <br /> The response obtained was &quot;you pick the provocation when you start trying to ride the wave,&quot; paraphrased.<br /> <br /> And then you get to change it if you succeed at riding the wave? How does that make sense?<br /> <br /> More importantly, that also means that you get to pick your frenzy target <i>whether or not </i>you succeed at riding the wave.<br /> <br /> Does that really seem like the intent? Anyone can frenzy at any time and set their goal and target freely, without needing to succeed at a roll, without even needing Coil of the Wyrm?<br /> <br /> If you attempt to Ride the Wave and pick your target/goal and then just... stop spending the Willpower required to keep rolling so that you deliberately fail, how is that any different from the Coil of the Wyrm that people were claiming is so much better than normal Ride the Wave? Because that's exactly what it lets you do. Start a frenzy with a target/goal of your choosing.<br /> <br /> I don't think &quot;well you don't get to pick a target/goal until you succeed&quot; is a valid option, either. Because then what if you fail? Does the ST just pick a random goal/target?<br /> <br /> I kind of think &quot;does this interpretation follow logically and consistently&quot; should be reason enough to accept or dismiss an interpretation of the rules. This &quot;you pick&quot; counter-argument actually makes me think a strong &quot;no&quot; on that front, in addition to the support the text gave in the quotes I provided earlier. In my opinion, at least.<br /> <br /> And again:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This desire does not have to align with the<br /> provocation. For example, if Victoria risks frenzy because she\u2019s<br /> starved, she might choose to kill Dominic instead of feeding. </div> </div> </div>&quot;The provocation.&quot; There is a provocation. It doesn't give any indication that a provocation is optional. &quot;The provocation&quot; gives a contrary indication; that there has to be one. It doesn't say &quot;does not have to align with any potential provocations&quot; or &quot;this desire can be anything the Kindred chooses&quot; thereby removing the implication that there has to be a provocation.<br /> <br /> Can someone provide an explanation for the provocation issue, supported by the text rather than conjecture or a previous, outdated edition of the game?<br /> <br /> I do grant CrimsonOwl's quote does provide some support for the point. I've always had a problem with that paragraph of the book, though. It directly contradicts everything before and after it, and is a pretty direct reading of 1e Requiem that doesn't take into account the fact that Vampires <i>aren't</i> always one step away from each others' throats anymore, with the changes to predatory aura. Feels really out of place in context.<br /> <br /> On that note, VtM allows Instinct rolls to Ride the Wave if you are on a Path that replaces Self-Control with Instinct. Characters with Instinct cannot even resist frenzy at all, unless the difficulty is below their Instinct, in which case they can resist without rolling but can't Ride the Wave. Characters with Self-Control can spend a willpower, I believe, to redirect their action for a turn. The game only calls it &quot;ride the wave&quot; explicitly for rolling Instinct during an existing Frenzy. I'm not sure what you're talking about with Dark Ages. Admittedly, I may be missing something. VtM isn't my area of expertise. But even with these rules supporting my point, I think it's really silly to base this argument on previous editions of VtR, and I think it's even sillier to base this argument on an entirely different game line that happens to be about vampires but otherwise has different themes, design philosophies, and mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T06:46:38-07:00","id":940065,"title":"","content":"Page 104, on resisting Frenzy:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dramatic failure on this roll results in frenzy, and the character cannot end the frenzy until she reaches a breaking point. If the Beast gets its desire, choose a new one. </div> </div> </div>Page 104 on Riding the Wave:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Treat any failure on this roll as a dramatic failure. </div> </div> </div>Yes, if you voluntarily Ride the Wave (instead of doing it as a response to a normal Frenzy), you choose the Beast's desire. If you fail, that's still the Beast's desire, but the Beast doesn't just stop after getting what it wants. The ST picks a new goal, and you keep going. You repeat this process until you hit a Breaking Point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T09:56:35-07:00","id":940122,"title":"","content":"I wish there was a polling tool on this site so we could at least do some democracy and get a consensus of - Yes you need to be provoked - or - No you do not need to be provoked. then we could just say well 72% of the people think this and we could just.. move on.<br /> <br /> Ultimately this is a game of interpretations, What-ifs, and guidelines, and suggested modifiers.and everyone plays differently. That is 100% ok as long as everyone is having fun. there are 100 different play styles and 100 different things to like. You just need to find the people who work for you to play with. Some people will work and some wont.. and that's ok.<br /> <br /> Only to strengthen that statement, I was told to build a character for a game. I built a daeva who was an MMA fighter with vigor and celerity.. and I was told I couldn't play it because it wasn't daeva enough...I knew right there, those people were not for me. So -shrugs- We just have to agree to disagree and try to have fun in whatever we are doing and move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":".  OMG spelling 07-30-2016, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T10:23:40-07:00","id":940135,"title":"","content":"I disagree with polling, in fact this is a specific, hard rules question that should have been specified in the book. It shouldn't even be up for interpretation and should have made it into the FAQ. The Errata for Requiem if I recall was only spelling and such changes rather than much clarification in the rules. There is a reason I asked for Developer input on this one specifically, I don't think its something that should even be remotely an issue, but somehow it is. It never even remotely occurred to me that you couldn't just ride the wave anytime you wanted. In fact if you can't it makes the Fighting style almost irrelevant unless you have the Coil.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T10:46:00-07:00","id":940139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=939910#post939910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't discourage Rose from commenting on this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't. It is really cool that she pays such close attention here. I even did a second paragraph clarifying that I want her to be present. My suggestion was that the forum users not stop at Author Intent; to really embrace the toolkit nature of the game and defy (the word of) God!<br /> <br /> But if I can't have my cake and eat it, I'd rather she stay. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T10:46:53-07:00","id":940140,"title":"","content":"It really does seem like you can spark up the wave to ride whenever you want. It just could have been worded better.<br /> <br /> But the game is malleable, and house rules and opinions leading to variant playstyles abundant. If Vitalis or others don't want to do it that way, then they shouldn't have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T11:37:39-07:00","id":940163,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think a poll would help anyone. If you're the sort who thinks at-will Riding the Wave makes no sense, seeing that 75% of the people on these forums disagree with you isn't going to make it make sense for you. If you're the sort who thinks at-will Riding the Wave is the more logical interpretation, seeing that 75% of the people on these forums think it doesn't make sense probably won't change your mind. If you're the sort who can see it working either way and just wants clarification of developer intent, you probably aren't going to care what the popular interpretation is. Discussion may not get the staunch supporters of either side to change their mind, but it can help sway someone who is on the fence one way or the other. I'd prefer to talk out the reasoning behind our interpretations and let people make an informed decision. If Rose wants to weigh in on the discussion, great! That's certainly very informative and should go a long way towards helping people decide if the intended functionality works for their group's needs or not. A poll only tells you what opinion is most popular among the people who decide to participate in the poll.<br /> <br /> All that said, I would be remiss not to point out that we <i>do</i> have a poll function. When you start a new thread, just hit the little graph icon at the top of the text box. You can have up to 10 options, and you can set it to allow multiple choice or just one, make votes public or hidden, and if you want it to stay open indefinitely or close after a set time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T11:59:17-07:00","id":940174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=940139#post940139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My suggestion was that the forum users not stop at Author Intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth--and I'm just one writer and one who wrote for VtM, not VtR, so maybe it shouldn't be worth all that much--I seriously agree. I've written this before, but I really, really believe that author's intent does not matter once the manuscript is out there. Y'all are very fortunate--and so are we, as writers--that we have a forum like this where we can answer and clarify things. When you're actually reading the book, I can't be over your shoulder saying, &quot;actually, what I MEANT is...&quot;<br /> <br /> Our work has to speak for itself. If it can't speak for itself, and if there's any grey area for something we did not intend to leave unclear, that's our fault, and we haven't done our job. Communication goes two ways. If you are putting forward a good-faith reading of my work and there's still grey for something that should be hard and clear, that's my fault as a writer.<br /> <br /> Just my opinion.<br /> <br /> I hope Rose does respond, if she wants to. I've become a lot more active on these forums myself since my work's been published, but that's my choice, and, again, it's a privilege we both have--readers get to ask us for clarification, and we get to clarify. But that's really a shift in practice. When it comes to texts of any sort (books, film, academic lectures, drawings), author's intent does not matter. What matters is what's on the page.<br /> <br /> (I'm also really hard on myself as a writer,and I approach this as an academic, and I'm only one OPP writer. This is Hayley's opinion, not necessarily anyone else's, but I personally feel pretty strongly about this.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 07-31-2016, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T13:04:56-07:00","id":940204,"title":"","content":"It's worth a great deal. And yes, you are hard on yourself, but who ever said that was a bad thing? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (most psychologists but they care about our happiness, not our ARTISTIC GLORY! :P )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T14:17:14-07:00","id":940253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=940163#post940163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't think a poll would help anyone. If you're the sort who thinks at-will Riding the Wave makes no sense, seeing that 75% of the people on these forums disagree with you isn't going to make it make sense for you. If you're the sort who thinks at-will Riding the Wave is the more logical interpretation, seeing that 75% of the people on these forums think it doesn't make sense probably won't change your mind. If you're the sort who can see it working either way and just wants clarification of developer intent, you probably aren't going to care what the popular interpretation is. Discussion may not get the staunch supporters of either side to change their mind, but it can help sway someone who is on the fence one way or the other. I'd prefer to talk out the reasoning behind our interpretations and let people make an informed decision. If Rose wants to weigh in on the discussion, great! .</div> </div> </div> </div>How can you use statistics to say statistics wont help? Is it really 75% think it's at anytime? We have talked, we have discussed. No one is budging.. but it might help future people to come in and see what we all came up with after the discussion...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T14:28:02-07:00","id":940257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=940253#post940253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can you use statistics to say statistics wont help? Is it really 75% think it's at anytime?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wha...? I just picked a random number, it could have been anything. I also used the same number for both sides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=940253#post940253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have talked, we have discussed. No one is budging.. but it might help future people to come in and see what we all came up with after the discussion...</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole point of my comment is that no one is going to budge even with a poll. The point of the discussion is not to convince you or me to change our minds, it's so that people who are unsure can see the arguments we each have made and decide for themselves which interpretation they want to use in their own games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T12:50:33-07:00","id":944471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=940257#post940257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point of my comment is that no one is going to budge even with a poll. The point of the discussion is not to convince you or me to change our minds, it's so that people who are unsure can see the arguments we each have made and decide for themselves which interpretation they want to use in their own games.</div> </div> </div> </div>This exactly. I have been reading the thread and see good reasoning on both sides. I am waiting to talk to my players about it when we start up a game and we will decide then, but it's good to see different arguments with supporting text that provide for both options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T17:11:51-07:00","id":944598,"title":"","content":"If I can be (slightly) facetious, it's &quot;riding the wave&quot;. You're not creating the wave. You still need a wave to ride.<br /> <br /> Using the Hulk as an imperfect comparison, Bruce Banner can't decide &quot;I'm going to hulk out here&quot;. He needs something to make him angry before the Beast wakes up.<br /> <br /> Using this approach doesn't stop vampires trying to deliberately wake their Beast. But I would want some external stimulus. Even if it means they go looking for it.<br /> <br /> We're all free to go our own way with this at the end of it. I think there are rules and interpretations which could use clarity, in the book. But, barring group arguments, this seems to me better left to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Is the Beast in your game something that comes when it's called, or is it a wild untameable animal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T17:24:20-07:00","id":944608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=944598#post944598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Beast in your game something that comes when it's called, or is it a wild untameable animal?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see what you mean, but wouldn't the Beast not jump at every opportunity it can get to get out of its cage? And since every time a Vampire decides to try to ride there is a chance it could get out... you get the picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T17:45:48-07:00","id":944613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lepaca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=944608#post944608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see what you mean, but wouldn't the Beast not jump at every opportunity it can get to get out of its cage? And since every time a Vampire decides to try to ride there is a chance it could get out... you get the picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe. <br /> <br /> But, and I'm just starting GM'ing Requiem (10-15 years after my last stint with Masquerade) and one thing I love about 2nd is it really empowers the &quot;Personal Horror&quot; that was almost lip service in 1st.<br /> <br /> And, what's more terrifying:<br /> - The thing that's always next to you, that you get used to. As they say, Familiarity Breeds Contempt.<br /> - The thing that lurks unseen. That comes out when you're most vulnerable, smelling blood and weakness like a shark. Ready to take over your body.<br /> <br /> Just because the Beast never leaves you doesn't mean it's always awake and trying to get out. It doesn't fight when you're strong. It fights when you're at your lowest ebb, and it's chain is at its weakest.<br /> <br /> The rest of the time it can sleep. And gather its strength...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T19:24:35-07:00","id":944661,"title":"","content":"If i might tag on another question to this thread. I was wondering what kind of actions you can take while frenzied/what character features you have available to you.<br /> <br /> For example. <br /> <br /> Could you use diciplines, like vigor or celerity? or even ones like dominate as long as they achieved the beasts desire in the most direct method possible<br /> <br /> Can you still use features such as fighting styles (obviously there is the riding the wave one but that works exclusively within frenzy so it is clear). but if you have heavy weapon style could you use those features to accomplish the beasts goal?<br /> <br /> And if it is the case you cant use fighting styles are you capable of using some weapons at all? obviously a club or sword could be feasible. but rapiers, guns etc require a level of thought to use rather than just SMASH.<br /> <br /> Basically the way im reading frenzy it is either:<br /> <br /> The beast takes over, its effectively a different character to you and therefore has none of the mental based features or ability to use diciplines etc.<br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> The beast drives you to achieve its goals in the most direct method possible. If its 'kill that guy' and you have a weapon in hand you can use your skills to achieve it. If you dont then you wont waste time drawing a weapon but will try to beat them with your fists and teeth? (but this does prevent you using non reflexive diciplines except in niche circumstances).<br /> <br /> And lastly im sure I read somewhere the vampires bite does leathal damage to other vampires. But looking through I cant see that anywhere, am I just going crazy? or if not could somebody give me a page reference for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T20:49:42-07:00","id":944679,"title":"","content":"Whoo boy, this is probably going to be another long and heated one.<br /> <br /> One thing is explicitly clear in the text. The Beast has no patience for forethought - it attempts to accomplish its goal by the most direct means possible. There are a lot of conflicting opinions on what exactly constitutes the most direct means possible.<br /> <br /> What I do? I leave the player in control of their character, but I tell them they can't take any action that doesn't directly advance the Beast's goal. Anything else is fair game. If Dominate directly helps you get what the Beast wants? Go ahead and use Dominate. A simple glance, a point of Vitae, and a growled &quot;out of my way&quot; seems like a perfectly reasonable thing to do if the Beast wants to escape. But if it wants to feed, dominating your would-be victim to hold still is one extra step between your fangs and their throat, and the Beast ain't got time for that. The Beast wants to kill? Go ahead and use the Carving maneuver of Kindred Dueling with your Fighting Finessed rapier. But the Warding Stance maneuver of Great Weapon Fighting Style is too defensive for the Beast to care about in a fight.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm aware that my interpretation is on the more liberal side. Some people prefer not to allow any Disciplines or Fighting Styles at all. Some people prefer to allow certain Disciplines and Styles and disallow others. I prefer my approach because it keeps the majority of the power in the player's hands. They decide for themselves what they think their characters' own Beasts would or wouldn't do, and I have a very simple metric for determining if I need to veto an action. Does it move the character closer to accomplishing the Beast's goals? If yes, it's fine. If no, tell the player that action requires too much forethought to work while Frenzying. I very rarely find myself needing to veto actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-05-2016, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T21:42:36-07:00","id":944693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=944679#post944679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoo boy, this is probably going to be another long and heated one.<br /> <br /> One thing is explicitly clear in the text. The Beast has no patience for forethought - it attempts to accomplish its goal by the most direct means possible. There are a lot of conflicting opinions on what exactly constitutes the most direct means possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>haha. Yeah. I Agree with you there that lots of people interpret this differently. I KNOW there is a huge thread about this already. Somewhere...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=944679#post944679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I do? I leave the player in control of their character, but I tell them they can't take any action that doesn't directly advance the Beast's goal. Anything else is fair game. If Dominate directly helps you get what the Beast wants? Go ahead and use Dominate. A simple glance, a point of Vitae, and a growled &quot;out of my way&quot; seems like a perfectly reasonable thing to do if the Beast wants to escape. But if it wants to feed, dominating your would-be victim to hold still is one extra step between your fangs and their throat, and the Beast ain't got time for that. The Beast wants to kill? Go ahead and use the Carving maneuver of Kindred Dueling with your Fighting Finessed rapier. But the Warding Stance maneuver of Great Weapon Fighting Style is too defensive for the Beast to care about in a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tell my players that &quot;you are in a hunger/kill/fear frenzy&quot; and they usually take it from there. Let loose without much directing. I actually havent had any players try to dominate or majesty to get out of situations... I know that when I play in a frenzy.. I dont do any of that either. After reading your examples, Charlaquin, I think that in <i>most </i>cases we would rule the same way.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said:<br /> <br /> If I were in a fear frenzy and needed to run.. I would not dominate and tell someone to get out of my way, because it is not an &quot;extreme response, usually meaning a blood-soaked frenzy&quot; Now hitting them or just down right plowing them over as you run.. That is extreme and violent.<br /> <br /> I dont allow my players a ton of control ( which none of them even try to take ) because frenzy is ( &quot; the vampire risks losing control of her Beast.&quot; ) the very definition of your character losing control. I play my frenzies Violent and messy. not calm and collected ( like dominate or majesty would be or even Obfuscate. ) Taking the time to dominate, then issuing the command, even trying to think of command to me says that it's too much forethought. Too much effort.. where as swinging your fist, or the nearest object at the person in the way.. to me is what a &quot;terrified animal' would do. ((( ever been so angry or scared you cant think of words?? )))<br /> <br /> <br /> This section from the book is really where it's at for me:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;While frenzied, the vampire does everything in her power<br /> to accomplish the Beast\u2019s desires. <b>She does so with immediate,<br /> forceful, and destructive abandon.</b> If there\u2019s someone in the<br /> way, she throws him or decks him. If she\u2019s hungry, she bites the<br /> closest thing to her mouth. That said, the Beast isn\u2019t stupid.<br /> It\u2019s capable of doing the kinds of things an enraged, terrified,<br /> or starving animal predator is, and it will lash out with the<br /> predatory aura if that will help sate it.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> <br /> Immediate. Forceful. Destructive. Abandon.<br /> with the choices Fight. Flight. Or Feed<br /> <br /> I let anything that is Immediate = resilience. vigor, celerity, protean, lashing out, healing, physical intensity ect<br /> <br /> Forceful and Destructive = Violent actions, punching kicking, biting, ect / or running away in the most direct quickest way possible. Dominating/charming or whatever to get out the door is not the quickest when simply running past the thing in your way is there...<br /> <br /> Doing these things with Abandon usually means it's reckless, careless of the consequences. So, fighting styles where it would require you to really put some thought into what you are doing I wouldnt let go through, but say if you had to drop all your defense to get more dice... that's really saying you dont give a F.. if you get hit. which is ok.<br /> <br /> if it's a fighting style where you are trying to be cool and calm , do this to do that, which causes this.. then I wouldnt let it go. ( but again. None of my players have ever asked to do anything super complicated while in a frenzy )<br /> <br /> You are effectively a rabid beast that wants something and wants it now... not later.<br /> <br /> Again. That's just me ( and seemed to go without even saying within my groups )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-06-2016, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T22:08:05-07:00","id":944702,"title":"","content":"I don't agree that Dominate is necessarily calm and collected, nor that it can't be immediate, forceful, destructive, and abandoned. But I don't really have the energy, nor the inclination to defend that stance at the moment.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, what should be possible or not possible in Frenzy is a highly subjective matter, on the order of D&amp;D alignment interpretations. As long as you use your best judgment and apply your rulings consistently, you're doing it right. For me, that means looking at results, not motivation, following the &quot;does this action bring the character closer to getting the Beast's goal?&quot; heuristic, and erring on the permissive side. If something else works for you, do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-06-2016, 01:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T22:16:14-07:00","id":944707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=944702#post944702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree that Dominate is necessarily calm and collected, nor that it can't be immediate, forceful, destructive, and abandoned. But I don't really have the energy, nor the inclination to defend that stance at the moment.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, what should be possible or not possible in Frenzy is a highly subjective matter, on the order of D&amp;D alignment interpretations. As long as you use your best judgment and apply your rulings consistently, you're doing it right. For me, that means looking at results, not motivation, following the &quot;does this action bring the character closer to getting the Beast's goal?&quot; heuristic, and erring on the permissive side. If something else works for you, do it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No no. I get it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Your point is totally valid. I was just explaining why I think the way I do. And I totally understand that not everyone thinks the way I do. I am just supporting my claims with details and text.<br /> <br /> I am with you completely, if it works for your group, go with it. Whatever that &quot;It&quot; is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T14:20:13-07:00","id":945060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=944679#post944679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I do? I leave the player in control of their character, but I tell them they can't take any action that doesn't directly advance the Beast's goal. Anything else is fair game. If Dominate directly helps you get what the Beast wants? Go ahead and use Dominate. A simple glance, a point of Vitae, and a growled &quot;out of my way&quot; seems like a perfectly reasonable thing to do if the Beast wants to escape. But if it wants to feed, dominating your would-be victim to hold still is one extra step between your fangs and their throat, and the Beast ain't got time for that. The Beast wants to kill? Go ahead and use the Carving maneuver of Kindred Dueling with your Fighting Finessed rapier. But the Warding Stance maneuver of Great Weapon Fighting Style is too defensive for the Beast to care about in a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that metric, dominating someone into stepping out of your way seems like a step further from shoving them out yourself. See the paradox?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T14:24:00-07:00","id":945061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=945060#post945060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By that metric, dominating someone into stepping out of your way seems like a step further from shoving them out yourself. See the paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really? They both get the person out of your way in the same amount of time, what do I care if they used a Discipline to do it?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Doh! Issuing a command has to be done on a different turn than than the turn you use Mesmerize, doesn't it? Sorry, my LARP background is showing. By tabletop RAW, I would not allow that because it does require an extra step. My bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-06-2016, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T14:33:08-07:00","id":945067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=945061#post945061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really? They both get the person out of your way in the same amount of time, what do I care if they used a Discipline to do it?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Doh! Issuing a command has to be done on a different turn than than the turn you use Mesmerize, doesn't it? Sorry, my LARP background is showing. By tabletop RAW, I would not allow that because it does require an extra step. My bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it literally takes twice as long to captivate the victim's attention and violate their will than just trying to shove them out of the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T14:39:00-07:00","id":945070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=945067#post945067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it literally takes twice as long to captivate the victim's attention and violate their will than just trying to shove them out of the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm still too used to thinking in terms of how things would play out in a LARP, where turns pretty much only matter in combat. You're totally right that using Mezmerize doesn't immediately advance the Beast's goals, I just forget that Mezmerize and Command are supposed to be separate actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T18:40:10-07:00","id":945209,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think so long as it lines up most directly with the beasts immediate wishes ill allow diciplines and styles. <br /> <br /> I think something like obfuscate is legitimate if you were flee frenzying from someone, its effectively cowering and hiding to escape and the most effective way to vanish. <br /> <br /> Im assuming as nobody chipped in about the vampires bite doing Lethal damage to other vampires i was simply misremembering it then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T18:43:31-07:00","id":945211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wunderkid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=945209#post945209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im assuming as nobody chipped in about the vampires bite doing Lethal damage to other vampires i was simply misremembering it then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm pretty sure it does. Sorry I forgot to address that part. I'll be back with a page number asap.<br /> <br /> EDIT: page 94. &quot;When feeding violently, a vampire\u2019s fangs act as 0L weapons that use the Brawl Skill. That is to say, on a successful attack, they cause lethal damage equal to their successes, even to Kindred.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-06-2016, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T03:18:59-07:00","id":945384,"title":"","content":"I'm going to toss in my two cents here for a moment. Why does it matter if it takes two turns to activate Dominate? The Beast is more than capable of using the Predator Auras during a frenzy. It really takes two turns at least for those to show any effect - a set up of actually inflicting the Aura, then next turn actually doing whatever the aura was set up to do. And, remember, Dominate/Nightmare/Majesty are basically upgraded versions of the Competative/Beastial/Wanton auras. Doesn't that mean that its well within the Beast's ability to set things at least for the duration of a single Instant Action? <br /> <br /> Also, on the matter of fangs, there's Riding the Wave Style, Ravage (\u2022). The fangs become 1L weapons while Riding the Wave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T07:43:32-07:00","id":945452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wunderkid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=945209#post945209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I think so long as it lines up most directly with the beasts immediate wishes ill allow diciplines and styles.<br /> <br /> I think something like obfuscate is legitimate if you were flee frenzying from someone, its effectively cowering and hiding to escape and the most effective way to vanish.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about obfuscate after the fact. I think I would allow that one to a fear frenzy, but not to set up an ambush for a kill frenzy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=945384#post945384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to toss in my two cents here for a moment. Why does it matter if it takes two turns to activate Dominate? The Beast is more than capable of using the Predator Auras during a frenzy. It really takes two turns at least for those to show any effect - a set up of actually inflicting the Aura, then next turn actually doing whatever the aura was set up to do. And, remember, Dominate/Nightmare/Majesty are basically upgraded versions of the Competative/Beastial/Wanton auras. Doesn't that mean that its well within the Beast's ability to set things at least for the duration of a single Instant Action?.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure if you mean for someone to answer that question or not, but I think it does matter as it's not &quot;Immediate&quot; like the book says. The examples of what you're capable of are all 1 turn things. All things that are &quot;right now&quot;. In that same breath,<br /> if you can take the time to dominate in a frenzy ( say a hunger frenzy ) tell them to hold still, then go bite them ( which would be 3 turns RAW ) why does the example say &quot;You bite the closest thing to your mouth&quot;? That implies to me.. RIGHT NOW. you turn and bite. Sure it might have the same end goal, but frenzy isnt about having that control to take your time and think about what wont get you in trouble and what wont hurt the other person. It's very literally the loss of control.<br /> <br /> Also it says that you can &quot;lash out&quot; Which is an actual thing with mechanics, it doesn't actually say anything about using disciplines which have a whole different set of mechanics thought they are derived from the same thing, the aura. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (Side note. I did mention it took 2x as long to mez and command as part of why I didnt allow it. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T08:29:29-07:00","id":945474,"title":"","content":"You know, at this point, I\u2019m glad the book isn't prescriptive. It's really evident many of us have completely different views on what the Beast is/means. And that\u2019s totally fine. We all have the right to play our games our way.<br /> <br /> What the Beast means to me:<br /> The Beast doesn\u2019t negotiate. It doesn't speak. It isn\u2019t sophisticated. It is (at the very least) a savage animal. It kills; it feeds; it flees. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m allowing all physical Disciplines, without a second thought. I can see the Beast using Protean, to draw its claws, etc.<br /> Outside of that though, I don't think I want to allow it to use any others. I\u2019d think about Obfuscate to flee.<br /> As for Predatory Aura, the book OK\u2019s it, and so do I. It's different to Dominate et al, because it is a primal, wordless, animalistic threat/challenge. It\u2019s terrifying the gazelle to run before you chase it.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve talked to my players about \u201chow can we make this seem like we\u2019re playing vampires and not Supers-with-Fangs\u201d, something we all felt with Masquerade.<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m endeavouring to Direct their approach (as, about to be embraced, vampires):<br /> Think of yourself not as a vampire.<br /> Think of yourself as a human brain in a vampire body.<br /> Don\u2019t think of the Beast as your dark subconscious. Or as a part of you.<br /> Think of the Beast as an alien entity in your brain that waits to overpower your mind and take over your body. An alien that only has wants and hungers.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d just watched \u201cUnder the Skin\u201d and \u201cRabid\u201d which informed my viewpoint.<br /> <br /> I want this part of the game, certainly in their early days, to be about the Personal Horror of what they have become. And the Beast is my Poster Boy for the whole concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","user":"FutureBondVillain","date":". 08-07-2016, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T09:16:33-07:00","id":945490,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12158\" data-vbnamecard=\"12158\">FutureBondVillain</a>: if you really want to focus on the personal horror aspect, and you want the Beast to be the iconic expression of that, I would really recommend <i>not</i> running the Beast as a separate, alien consciousness. If it's alien, it's by definition not personal. It's something from outside, something other, and while it might be sharing your body and fighting for control of your mind, it's distinctly not <i>you</i>.<br /> <br /> Now, the idea of having your body, your thoughts, and your control invaded by this atavistic entity is horrifying, to be sure, but it's not <i>personal</i> horror. It's still John Carpenter's first type of story, the one where evil comes from &quot;out there&quot;. Even if it's physically in the same space with you, it doesn't <i>come from</i> within you. It comes from the curse, or from the Strix that first created it, or from what ever hellish pit it first slithered out of. It's not &quot;what have I done?&quot;, it's &quot;the Devil made me do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, there's nothing wrong with that kind of horror, and it'll certainly get you away from &quot;superheroes with fangs&quot;. But if what you really want from the Beast is personal horror, then the Beast has to be just as much you as the Man. That's John Carpenter's second type of story, where evil comes from &quot;in here.&quot; Vampires might blame their actions in Frenzy on something the call &quot;The Beast&quot;, but it's a lie they tell themselves to shift the blame. They tell stories about the Strix making a deal with their progenitors and creating the Beast, but it's a way to comfort themselves, to give an external origin to something they don't want to admit they're fully capable of all on their own.<br /> <br /> If you really want the Beast to embody personal horror, then you want it to be the vampire's own darkest instincts and desires, free of inhibition or limitations placed on it by the self-judgmental Man. Pure Id, with no interference from Ego or Super-Ego. You want Frenzy to be what happens not when something else takes over, but when the vampire herself lets go.<br /> <br /> That's what makes the difference between the two types of horror. Are you afraid of the monsters (even the monsters inside your head)? Or are you afraid of yourself? Both are valid choices, but I personally find the latter far more compelling.<br /> <br /> That's part of why I prefer to err on the permissive side with Frenzy. It's not the primary reason (that would be ease of use), but it is a contributing factor. Because I don't like to run the Frenzy as what happens when an animalistic conscious that isn't capable of the same higher order thought as you takes over. I like to run Frenzy it as exactly what you would do, if you stopped giving a shit about the consequences and just took whatever you wanted by the most immediate means possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-07-2016, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T09:33:21-07:00","id":945498,"title":"","content":"That's also part of why I like Riding the<br /> Wave to be possible at any time. You don't need provocation, you just need to let yourself go. The only question is, once you've let go, are you going to be able to reel yourself back in? And that's why success on the Riding the Wave goal lets you stop after achieving one goal and failure causes you to ride the Frenzy from one goal to the next until you hit a Breaking Point. You get a taste of that freedom that comes from releasing your Ego and just taking what you want, and you don't want to give it up. You keep going, you see something else you want and you take that too. And so on, until you finally do something that snaps your Super-Ego back into action. When you reach that point where you look at yourself and say &quot;Dear God, what have I done?&quot; then and only then does a botched Ride end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T10:01:51-07:00","id":945515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=945452#post945452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure if you mean for someone to answer that question or not, but I think it does matter as it's not &quot;Immediate&quot; like the book says. The examples of what you're capable of are all 1 turn things. All things that are &quot;right now&quot;. In that same breath,<br /> if you can take the time to dominate in a frenzy ( say a hunger frenzy ) tell them to hold still, then go bite them ( which would be 3 turns RAW ) why does the example say &quot;You bite the closest thing to your mouth&quot;? That implies to me.. RIGHT NOW. you turn and bite. Sure it might have the same end goal, but frenzy isnt about having that control to take your time and think about what wont get you in trouble and what wont hurt the other person. It's very literally the loss of control.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ehhh.... my point is that its the same number of turns / actions for biting in either case. Not twice as long, exactly the same amount. So, if you're trying to judge the actions by the amount of time it takes, then its a complete wash since both methods take an equal amount of time - three turns, or two with an exceptional success on a certain roll. A permissive GM might even allow simple Mesmerization to have someone go passive, and feed on them, without the need of a command as an instant action. <br /> <br /> I actually agree that using Dominate feels off in a frenzy to me (too human-like of an action), but the argument that it takes too long is simply and provably untrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T10:22:53-07:00","id":945530,"title":"","content":"Hi Charly. I appreciate the (time and) thoughts. I think I understand where you're coming from. We definitely seem on opposite ends of the spectrum when it comes to our approaches to the Beast, and what we want it to mean. Though our goals seem very similar. This discourse is certainly helpful to me, in clarifying my own take. So, thanks for that.<br /> <br /> I've ran the Beast the more traditional way in Masquerade. And honestly, it always felt like more of an annoyance to the players. Never something horrible. Maybe part of that is my groups approach (me included).<br /> <br /> Personal Horror is a funny word. It can mean different things to different people, I think. Ultimately I think this approach is still personal precisely because it is not outside of you. It is within you.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s internal, and personal horror, because whether the Beast is you or not, you are responsible for it. You are allowing it to exist. To perpetrate horrible crimes. Because you can stop it at any moment by walking out into the sun. You chose not to. Therefore you are responsible. <br /> <br /> And hell, maybe this whole \u201cit\u2019s not me, I didn't do it\u201d IS just a comforting lie you tell yourself.<br /> <br /> So, to be clear, I'm not (necessarily) saying my Beast is an alien entity *literally*. But I am strongly suggesting that thought as an approach to roleplaying it (a Director to my Actors, as it were). It doesn't have to be literally true. My wording above is deliberate and fine, \u201c*think of it* as an alien entity\u201d. It\u2019s a way to free the player of the responsibility in the moment. Because the Beast has no conscience. None.<br /> <br /> The problem, when we think of it as an \u201cus\u201d, is it encourages thoughts of \u201cI wouldn't do that\u201d. And that thought is a significant step towards a controlled beast that can limit its actions. I don\u2019t want (any) of their conscience (as characters or players) kicking in. I don\u2019t want them to feel in control. It\u2019s hard to feel horror when you have control.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller I feel no need to decide if it even is, or is not, alien. Because you don\u2019t need to understand the Beast. No one does. I\u2019d say no vampire has ever known where it comes from, or what it really is. Because what it really is is a metaphor for the horrible things we people can do. And the more I can empower that the happier I am likely to be with the results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T17:58:58-07:00","id":945775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=945515#post945515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ehhh.... my point is that its the same number of turns / actions for biting in either case. Not twice as long, exactly the same amount. So, if you're trying to judge the actions by the amount of time it takes, then its a complete wash since both methods take an equal amount of time - three turns, or two with an exceptional success on a certain roll. A permissive GM might even allow simple Mesmerization to have someone go passive, and feed on them, without the need of a command as an instant action.<br /> <br /> I actually agree that using Dominate feels off in a frenzy to me (too human-like of an action), but the argument that it takes too long is simply and provably untrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure where you're getting three turns for not dominating to bite.<br /> <br /> Outside of frenzy, you grapple, then you bite. Two turns at most.<br /> <br /> Inside a frenzy, you can grab and bite in the same turn. It's considerably faster to not Dominate first if you're trying to feed in a frenzy.<br /> <br /> Staring people down and giving orders is something you do before you frenzy. Once you're in the middle of it, talking out your desires with your enemy really doesn't seem thematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T20:18:33-07:00","id":945867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=945515#post945515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ehhh.... my point is that its the same number of turns / actions for biting in either case. Not twice as long, exactly the same amount. So, if you're trying to judge the actions by the amount of time it takes, then its a complete wash since both methods take an equal amount of time - three turns, or two with an exceptional success on a certain roll. A permissive GM might even allow simple Mesmerization to have someone go passive, and feed on them, without the need of a command as an instant action. <br /> <br /> I actually agree that using Dominate feels off in a frenzy to me (too human-like of an action), but the argument that it takes too long is simply and provably untrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>As mania pointed out. Raw. 1 mesmerize, 2 command, 3 grapple/feed. ( three turns ) <br /> <br /> Frenzied vampire: 1 grapple and feed. ( Same single turn. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-07-2016, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T00:30:17-07:00","id":945998,"title":"","content":"The book states that the Beast is not silly, it's smart. In my interpretation this means that she will do anything to accomplish her goal but not in a too dangerous way. I'll try to make some examples of scenario to make my point of view more clear:<br /> <br /> Hunger Frenzy: The vampire lurks in the shadows at a big group of people; she wants feed, now. But attacking all of them would means DEAD (supposing they will not run away, it's just an hypothetical scenario; you can replace normal people with the presence of many police). So, the frenzied vampire could use:<br /> - Obfuscate to feed between them unnoticed. <br /> - Staring the strongest man (even he is her brother) with a twinkle in the eyes and commanding him: Come with me. Then feed.<br /> - Pace the room with her unnatural charm and let someone fallow her in the same way of dominate.<br /> - Using Vigor and celerity if she doesen't have any other more viable disciplines.<br /> <br /> In any case she will feed in the more direct and smart way possible according to her powers. Note that I' said: more direct way possible. This doesen't means go inside and bite everyone in the first turn if this would mean death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-08-2016, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T04:46:56-07:00","id":946074,"title":"","content":"Really. There is another way to pit this question.<br /> <br /> Do you think its cooler to have vampires carry around lighters and look at them before riding the wave or do you think its silly? If you think its silly, let your players ride the wave when they please. I lean in the latter camp.<br /> <br /> I mean ultimately you can just think insults to yourself (or your beast) to rile it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T05:58:57-07:00","id":946103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946074#post946074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really. There is another way to pit this question. Do you think its cooler to have vampires carry around lighters and look at them before riding the wave or do you think its silly? If you think its silly, let your players ride the wave when they please. I lean in the latter camp. I mean ultimately you can just think insults to yourself (or your beast) to rile it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, disagree. But I also wouldn't have a PC/NPC flick lighters at people to force frenzy checks.<br /> <br /> You can disagree with a silly way of triggering the beast without saying Riding the Wave is always on. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T08:06:54-07:00","id":946172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=945998#post945998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book states that the Beast is not silly, it's smart. In my interpretation this means that she will do anything to accomplish her goal but not in a too dangerous way. I'll try to make some examples of scenario to make my point of view more clear:<br /> <br /> Hunger Frenzy: The vampire lurks in the shadows at a big group of people; she wants feed, now. But attacking all of them would means DEAD (supposing they will not run away, it's just an hypothetical scenario; you can replace normal people with the presence of many police). So, the frenzied vampire could use:<br /> - Obfuscate to feed between them unnoticed.<br /> - Staring the strongest man (even he is her brother) with a twinkle in the eyes and commanding him: Come with me. Then feed.<br /> - Pace the room with her unnatural charm and let someone fallow her in the same way of dominate.<br /> - Using Vigor and celerity if she doesen't have any other more viable disciplines.<br /> <br /> In any case she will feed in the more direct and smart way possible according to her powers. Note that I' said: more direct way possible. This doesen't means go inside and bite everyone in the first turn if this would mean death.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To clarify, the book states it's not stupid, but it doesnt say it's smart. It says &quot;<i>It\u2019s capable of doing the kinds of things an enraged, terrified, or starving animal predator is.&quot; </i>Does the starving tiger care if there are 10 humans? It's out numbered and they have guns. No it doesnt, it tries to get that 1 human. Does the terrified Lion care that there are 4 people in front of the open door. The window is there, unlocked, but he would have to open it first.. he goes through the door, pushing anything out of the way. Frenzy is the very loss of control down to your base instincts, fight, flight or feed. <br /> <br /> All of your examples ( except vigor and celerity ) show collected thought, which frenzy is the opposite of.<br /> <br /> <br /> For example.<br /> <br /> Vampire X has kidnapped your touchstone. You are to meet him somewhere to do the exchange. You show up alone, thinking he is going to be alone. You find out you are outnumbered 6 to 1. Vamp X killed your touchstone ( you fail all the rolls ) And frenzy. But wait. You dont attack because that would be silly 6 to 1, you will lose. But you're in a kill frenzy. You want Vamp X's head. You are frenzied. Do you walk away and plan a better time because now you would be dead...<br /> <br /> Same as your scenario. Attacking too many people to feed would mean some of them might hurt you, or you would break the masquerade, so therefore you dont do it or you bide your time and wait for a better opportunity? <br /> <br /> The Prince orders you to watch the execution of your ghoul. ( you fail the roll to not frenzy ) but you dont try to attack him because... it's the prince and that would be death.<br /> <br /> You wake up one night after a really great time and you forgot to feed, you slip into a hunger frenzy, but the only person there is your lover. Do you go looking for someone else because you might kill them? Do you feed nicely, taking your time, just a little nip at the wrist because you wouldnt want to accidentally tear their throat out?<br /> <br /> This might just be me, but I would say that you are ignoring the effects of frenzy if you choose not to do something because it might have bad consequences... ( I think that's the whole point of frenzy. To have the possibility of really bad consequences. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T08:48:20-07:00","id":946192,"title":"","content":"Yes I agree with you that if the prince provokes your frenzy you'd attack him even if it is death. Same for the lover you'd feed on. I just means that, if is there a way to obtain the goal that provokes your frenzy that can save your life, you cangot trought that way. Without thinking to your morality or anything else just your survivability, that is the primary instinct of any animal predator. <br /> A starved lion would never attack another pride of lions to steal their food. In my opinion...<br /> A frenzy vampire it's just a monster that want to obtain his goal without thinking anything else then his own will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T09:00:08-07:00","id":946203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946172#post946172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire X has kidnapped your touchstone. You are to meet him somewhere to do the exchange. You show up alone, thinking he is going to be alone. You find out you are outnumbered 6 to 1. Vamp X killed your touchstone ( you fail all the rolls ) And frenzy. But wait. You dont attack because that would be silly 6 to 1, you will lose. But you're in a kill frenzy. You want Vamp X's head. You are frenzied. Do you walk away and plan a better time because now you would be dead...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow Obfuscate/Nightmare/Majesty/Animalism, anything that'd improve your immediate odds.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same as your scenario. Attacking too many people to feed would mean some of them might hurt you, or you would break the masquerade, so therefore you dont do it or you bide your time and wait for a better opportunity? </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate and chomp, or Nightmare to cull the herd.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Prince orders you to watch the execution of your ghoul. ( you fail the roll to not frenzy ) but you dont try to attack him because... it's the prince and that would be death. </div> </div> </div>In this case, I'd say the goal isn't to kill the Prince, but to rescue the ghoul. Small nitpick, and I'm not sure which Disciplines I'd allow while frenzying in this scenario. Probably the same ones as in the first example.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You wake up one night after a really great time and you forgot to feed, you slip into a hunger frenzy, but the only person there is your lover. Do you go looking for someone else because you might kill them? Do you feed nicely, taking your time, just a little nip at the wrist because you wouldnt want to accidentally tear their throat out? </div> </div> </div>Nope, they'd be screwed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T09:21:55-07:00","id":946213,"title":"","content":"\u201cthe Beast is as good at coming up with a plan as a crazed shit-house rat.\u201d p. 59<br /> <br /> \u201cthe Beast goads her to immediate and extreme response.\u201d p. 103 (Frenzy)<br /> <br /> \u201cimmediate, forceful and destructive abandon.\u201d p. 104 (the Frenzy)<br /> \u201cthe Beast isn\u2019t stupid. It's capable of doing the kind of things an enraged, terrified, or starving animal predator is\u201d p. 104<br /> <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know where people are getting their interpretations from. They certainly seem to be taking the Beast as an enraged animal and turning it into a thinking, controlled pet who helps them.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a wild animal. It wants. And it wants now. It doesn't come up with plans (quote 1). It isn\u2019t any smarter than an animal (look at the end of quote 4 re: the Beast isn\u2019t stupid). <br /> It doesn't even seem to be capable of working out \u201cwhat\u2019s the best way I can achieve my goal.\u201d It doesn't think about danger. It just knows what it wants and goes and gets it. Immediately and extremely.<br /> <br /> There is no mention of fine discipline usage anywhere (which is a message itself). There is mention of Predatory Aura (an animalistic response). Are Majesty, Dominate animalistic responses? Hell no.<br /> Physical disciples I\u2019m fine with because they are physical, direct and forceful. Like an animal is.<br /> <br /> Really people seem to be getting into the old-Path mentality \u201cstuff I was going to do anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> If you can\u2019t get horror from the Beast then I don't know where you're getting it from. Because if the Beast isn\u2019t something that scares your characters (hell, your players) then I don\u2019t see the point of it. It surely becomes \u201cmy super powered little friend\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:13:18-07:00","id":946256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946213#post946213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no mention of fine discipline usage anywhere (which is a message itself).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no mention of gross Discipline usage either. The section is more proscriptive, saying what the beast can't do, which tells me that since Disciplines aren't mentioned, they aren't something the beast can't do, unless they violate one of the other proscriptions. That's why I say if it takes forethought it's out. If it brings you closer to your goal, it's in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946213#post946213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is mention of Predatory Aura (an animalistic response). Are Majesty, Dominate animalistic responses? Hell no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to have to strongly disagree with you there. Majesty is a primal, instinctive allure. Dominate relies on the dominant and submissive dynamic between pack animals. These powers are manipulations of the Predatory Aura, and the Predatory Aura is nothing if not animalistic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946213#post946213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physical disciples I\u2019m fine with because they are physical, direct and forceful. Like an animal is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Animals are more than just that though. People in these conversations often don't give animals enough credit. They aren't calculating, but they are intelligent in other ways, even when starved, frightened, or provoked. A human with no inhibitions is very much an animal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946213#post946213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can\u2019t get horror from the Beast then I don't know where you're getting it from. Because if the Beast isn\u2019t something that scares your characters (hell, your players) then I don\u2019t see the point of it. It surely becomes \u201cmy super powered little friend\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see where you're getting &quot;if you can use Dominate, it's not horror.&quot; The Beast is absolutely horrifying, but it is horror at what you are capable of when you let your instincts get the better of you, not horror at what another entity does when it has control of your body. And honestly, even for those who prefer &quot;the other&quot; interpretation of the Beast, I still fail to see how that other being capable of using Dominate makes it not horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-08-2016, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:23:26-07:00","id":946263,"title":"","content":"Someone said Majesty, Dominate and Nightmare are the expansions of the seductive, competitive and bestial aura respectively, so yes, they are animalistic response as much as predatory aura is according to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:26:37-07:00","id":946267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946263#post946263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone said Majesty, Dominate and Nightmare are the expansions of the seductive, competitive and bestial aura respectively, so yes, they are animalistic response as much as predatory aura is according to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it was <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:09:16-07:00","id":946297,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7079_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7079\" data-vbnamecard=\"7079\">Marcus</a><br /> <br /> While I do agree with you that Majesty, Dominate and Nightmare are extensions of the predatory aura, I do not agree that they are animalistic. I want to point out again that the book says that they can &quot;LASH OUT&quot; with the predatory aura not that they can use predatory auras. Those two phrases have entirely different meanings. Lashing out provokes a primal fight or flight response in your victim. The disciplines do not out right provoke that ( some can yes, but only specific ones, like majesty 3 provoking a frenzy )<br /> <br /> To say that everything a vampire does is animalistic is just not acurate. They are not animals. They have conscious thought. They can weight pros and cons and make choices. Where as the most primal base instincts are. Fight. Flight, and Feed... then deal with the consequences later.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4854\" data-vbnamecard=\"4854\">Justin Sane</a><br /> Lions will attack other lions for food, even when not starving, so take a starving lion who knows they will die without that food and they will attack anything in their way to get it.. not plan and wait for the other lions to leave( or nightmare them away ) or plot out some elaborate plan to safely get the food (or try to obfuscate to sneak it away). They will take it or die trying, damn the consequences. Doing any disciplines that put steps in between &quot;bite the closest thing to your mouth&quot; takes away from what frenzy is.<br /> <br /> A rabid dog does not care if it attacks it's master and the master might kill him for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also dont think that &quot;Rescue&quot; is one of the directives of Frenzy. You might try to rescue the ghoul before he is executed but I would think that is not done in the frenzy. You might frenzy and try to kill executioner before he swings the axe, but that is a fight frenzy. Rescue doesnt fit the &quot;fight, flight or feed&quot; theme of frenzy. Rescue implies too much conscious thought and planning for a frenzy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Frenzy is the very loss of control. It is reckless Immediate, destructive and forceful. Anything thoughtful, planned, patient or not dangerous is just not what frenzy is suppose to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a><br /> <br /> Majesty can be primal ( awe ), I do not think that Charming, Enthralling or shifting emotions (with green eyes ) shows primal thought. It shows a conscious effort to adjust things. It requires you to have an understanding of life and how it works ( empathy ) to manipulate it. Enraged, terrified, or starved animals lack that or lack the ability to care about that in that moment,<br /> <br /> Same with Dominate. Sure it is a &quot;I am alpha of the pack, bow to me&quot; sort of thing, but it requires finesse. Effort and thought, planning. What will you command them to say once they are yours? What is the best command to give in this situation? Even if that planning only extends to the next turn. You are still rationalizing your actions and considering the consequences. Which I think that starving, enraged, and terrified animals do not do.<br /> ( but I do see that you posted you wouldnt allow it because it puts those extra steps into getting what the beast wants )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:14:50-07:00","id":946300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946263#post946263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone said Majesty, Dominate and Nightmare are the expansions of the seductive, competitive and bestial aura respectively, so yes, they are animalistic response as much as predatory aura is according to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda think your turning a blind eye to the key word. Expansion/Extension doesn\u2019t mean \u201cthe same as\u201d. It means grew out of/comes from.<br /> <br /> Human speech is an extension of animal communication. It doesn\u2019t mean animals can talk. They are not the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:15:22-07:00","id":946302,"title":"","content":"I think we can all argue this until we\u2019re blue in the face. We all have our own desires of what we want the Beast to mean. And we can all twist words and sentences to mean what we want/think them to mean. <br /> <br /> I guess my point is, the Frenzy is completely open to interpretation. No doubt, this is the intention. We can all have the Beast in our games be as we want/think it to be. That's fine, and probably as it should be.<br /> <br /> You can have your vampires Dominate a command to \u201cgive me your blood\u201d.<br /> I\u2019ll have mine grab them by the arms and violently sink its teeth in their neck.<br /> <br /> And never the twain shall meet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:27:35-07:00","id":946311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946300#post946300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda think your turning a blind eye to the key word. Expansion/Extension doesn\u2019t mean \u201cthe same as\u201d. It means grew out of/comes from.<br /> <br /> Human speech is an extension of animal communication. It doesn\u2019t mean animals can talk. They are not the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Human talking is a complex comunication form, animal comunicates each other in a lot of way. <br /> Furthemore parrot can spelling human words but his is not comunication... so the human talk is just a form of animalistic comunication as other, just a lot more complex","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:43:33-07:00","id":946326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946302#post946302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can have your vampires Dominate a command to \u201cgive me your blood\u201d.<br /> I\u2019ll have mine grab them by the arms and violently sink its teeth in their neck.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'll let my 'starving lion' attack the weakest member of the pride, instead of just bull-rushing the first Alpha Female they see. And allow a Kindred to frenzy on the Prince's ghoul rather than the Prince when watching the mentioned execution as an eye for an eye. And allow someone to reload a gun so they can fire more and more bullets into their enemy. Or allow them to use Nightmare to scare away group to isolate a certain target.<br /> <br /> The beast isn't stupid. Suicide and using inferior tools - when you have better tools <i>that help get what you want - </i>play out as more ridiculous to me. I don't need a frenzied character to take the MOST enraged, bestial action possible. Just something that falls dramatically in that spectrum. If they get too logical-calculating over animal-cunning, I'll ask for a willpower spend, but otherwise letting players take the lead in roleplaying that moment isn't something I'm going to trounce on because they try and do it more effectively. I'm not going to drown myself in turn counters and initiative calculations for the most direct atrocity when there are already dramatic stakes on the line (the only time frenzy is appropriate).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T17:17:39-07:00","id":946557,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised people can't imagine something called &quot;Dominate&quot; being animalistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T17:51:55-07:00","id":946585,"title":"","content":"I think it's sort of being looked at from a narrow angle.<br /> <br /> If you're frenzying because you want blood, you're not likely to Dominate because you can just suck it out easier. But if you're frenzying because your touchstone was just kidnapped by an enemy, Dominating the mind of the closest person to find out where they've been taken is more likely. Providing you're frenzying because you want to get your touchstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T23:20:30-07:00","id":946765,"title":"","content":"For me, it's a simple matter of the fact that Dominate requires human speech. Human speech is not animalistic. The fact that it's not immediate has already been covered, but human speech is the Man, and the Man and the Beast are opposites. When Frenzying, the Beast is in control. Not the Man. That's the whole point. That's what Frenzy is.<br /> <br /> Lashing Out, as mentioned before, is both more directly related the Beast and does not require speech.<br /> <br /> Dominate is a more refined version of the Seductive Beast. The Beast itself is not refined. Neither is Frenzy.<br /> <br /> You might try to talk your way out of a situation before Fight or Flight hits, but once it hits there's no more talking.<br /> <br /> This is something they teach in martial arts. If you are talking, your focus for fight-or-flight is lessened. This is working against the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T04:31:52-07:00","id":946858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946765#post946765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something they teach in martial arts. If you are talking, your focus for fight-or-flight is lessened. This is working against the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is this statement applies to an awful lot.<ul><li>If you are (using a weapon), your focus for fight-or-flight is lessened. This is working against the Beast.</li> <li>If you are (remembering martial arts training), your focus for fight-or-flight is lessened. This is working against the Beast.</li> <li>If you are (looking for escape routes), your focus for fight-or-flight is lessened. This is working against the Beast.</li> </ul>Would you let a frenzied character use <b><i>every </i></b>tool/ability that the Man learned or trained in, or none at all? If you're not at one of these extremes, then we're just talking where to draw the line. A speech line isn't the end of the world, but I prefer to say if the action is something people are known to do while asleep or blackout drunk - it's something your beast can do. I think the Beast can use tools, even ones the man originally cultivated. <br /> <br /> If a Kindred frenzies behind the wheel of a car during a chase scene, I would totally let the person crash their car into the trigger/enemy as part of it. I wouldn't say they have to leap out of the car so they can run after the trigger like a dog joke cliche. <br /> <br /> You're running from a frenzied Kindred and - just by inches - make it into an elevator. It begins pounding on the doors as you hit the up button. Does the Kindred stay there pounding on the doors letting you get away, or is it cunning enough to understand the ding and the up arrow mean it should find the stairs and keep chasing you?<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm jaded from a lot of LARP experiences where frenzy is very throwaway and non-dramatic, but the absolute mindlessness takes away from the drama and horror for me. A parasite / alter-ego that can use your skills and even low-level knowledge to fuel its feed/flight/fight instincts - that's a much more intense aspect of personal horror from my perspective. A growled out Dominate command of 'Submit' or a use of Awe from the shadows to pull a kine in to its death - those are both dramatic and I feel thematic.<br /> <br /> If the player is being a cheese about it because they just don't like frenzy or the loss of complete protagonist control - that's a different issue. But I'm gonna solve that by talking to the player, not by spending a lot of time going through Merits and abilities and setting a flag for each one: 'Can use in Frenzy - Y/N'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T04:49:04-07:00","id":946863,"title":"","content":"Nevermind, I guess I imagined it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-09-2016, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T06:38:17-07:00","id":946913,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946557#post946557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised people can't imagine something called &quot;Dominate&quot; being animalistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's little of animalistic in the usual fashion that vampires hypnotize their victims to forfeit their will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946326#post946326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The beast isn't stupid. Suicide and using inferior tools - when you have better tools <i>that help get what you want - </i>play out as more ridiculous to me. I don't need a frenzied character to take the MOST enraged, bestial action possible. Just something that falls dramatically in that spectrum. If they get too logical-calculating over animal-cunning, I'll ask for a willpower spend, but otherwise letting players take the lead in roleplaying that moment isn't something I'm going to trounce on because they try and do it more effectively. I'm not going to drown myself in turn counters and initiative calculations for the most direct atrocity when there are already dramatic stakes on the line (the only time frenzy is appropriate).</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation is that, yes, the beast is stupid. Yes it is. It clearly is. It's called Frenzy for a reason. Not &quot;Blood possessed cunning demonhood&quot;. Higher functions are denied to you. You want to portray the seductive Beast whilst on Frenzy? You'll tear off the clothes of the girl on the stage while the ongoing effects of Majesty suggests to the audience that this is all part of the act. Pretty dramatic in my opinion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T08:02:48-07:00","id":946947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946913#post946913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My interpretation is that, yes, the beast is stupid. Yes it is. It clearly is. It's called Frenzy for a reason. Not &quot;Blood possessed cunning demonhood&quot;. Higher functions are denied to you. You want to portray the seductive Beast whilst on Frenzy? You'll tear off the clothes of the girl on the stage while the ongoing effects of Majesty suggests to the audience that this is all part of the act. Pretty dramatic in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, considering the book actively states the Beast isn't stupid, I'll agree to disagree. : )<br /> <br /> But your example clearly fits in my world as a dramatic frenzy <i>with discipline use</i> that makes perfect sense for the scene.<br /> <br /> Feel free to delineate which subsets of Base-10 Disciplines can be used and which ones can't in a frenzy, that's using the tool kit as intended. That particular granularity isn't too valuable to me. If the action both adds to the dramatics, gets you closer to what your beast wants, and especially is a more primal / guttural / primitive action than something your character would normally do? I'm not going to pull the trigger on taking over the character for not roleplaying frenzy accurately.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T13:39:23-07:00","id":947202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=946858#post946858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is this statement applies to an awful lot.<ul><li>If you are (using a weapon), your focus for fight-or-flight is lessened. This is working against the Beast.</li> <li>If you are (remembering martial arts training), your focus for fight-or-flight is lessened. This is working against the Beast.</li> <li>If you are (looking for escape routes), your focus for fight-or-flight is lessened. This is working against the Beast.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in your list has anything to do with what I said.<br /> <br /> You're not even being pedantic. You're just being deliberately counter-intuitive. This is a strawman at absolute best.<br /> <br /> It's part of self-defense training that you get your captor to talk so their reaction times are slowed down if they have you caught. Talking distracts the body. It takes a lot of focus. More than we really realize.<br /> <br /> Having a weapon in your hand takes no focus. Swinging your arm is swinging your arm with a weapon or not.<br /> <br /> Remembering martial arts training? Probably would. But the entire point of sparring and practicing martial arts is to make it part of muscle memory. It's reflex. It doesn't take any focus.<br /> <br /> Is it a reflexive part of muscle memory for you to look someone in the eye, imbue your glance with hypnotic properties, then tell them &quot;hold still&quot; whenever you're so hungry it puts the animal inside you into into a fight-or-flight response? If it were, go for it. But it's not. Because that's ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Looking for escape routes is the dumbest of all three examples. It's right in the name. &quot;Fight-or-<i>flight</i>&quot;. You can't run if you don't have anywhere to run to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T16:08:22-07:00","id":947297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave?p=947202#post947202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nothing in your list has anything to do with what I said. You're not even being pedantic. You're just being deliberately counter-intuitive. This is a strawman at absolute best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, you're getting a little hostile, but I'll try to clarify.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's part of self-defense training that you get your captor to talk so their reaction times are slowed down if they have you caught. Talking distracts the body. It takes a lot of focus. More than we really realize. [...] Is it a reflexive part of muscle memory for you to look someone in the eye, imbue your glance with hypnotic properties, then tell them &quot;hold still&quot; whenever you're so hungry it puts the animal inside you into into a fight-or-flight response? If it were, go for it. But it's not. Because that's ridiculous. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I don't see augmenting your voice (dominate) or presence (majesty / obfuscate) any different than the concentration needed to imbue your blood with augmented strength, speed or toughness or your body with Protean. You want to argue that carrying on a conversation takes focus, then I'm with you. Grunting out a one-or-two word command doesn't, so that's where you lose me. Breath control (aka the same monkey-power that lets us have language) is also a lot of muscle memory. It's used as shock absorption and power enhancement both in martial arts, as you clearly know.<br /> <br /> And yes, I say the beast is smart enough to use the best weapon they can bring to the table not just claw/claw/bite. It's Fight/Flight/Feed - you keep leaving off that last one. It's not so binary anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having a weapon in your hand takes no focus. Swinging your arm is swinging your arm with a weapon or not. </div> </div> </div>Takes no focus if you've trained with it, in my experience. When you first start, though, it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remembering martial arts training? Probably would. But the entire point of sparring and practicing martial arts is to make it part of muscle memory. It's reflex. It doesn't take any focus. </div> </div> </div>Completely agree. I think you're just underestimating what can be done reflexively. And look, I'm not saying more 'cerebral' disciplines are right in every situation. But I'm also not going to say they're never right in <i>any </i>situation.<br /> <br /> If you have a high defense victim consistently dodging your frenzied attacks, I'd absolutely allow you to &quot;Heel&quot; at them to get what your beast wants. If your Ventrue Knight with a ton of fighting styles voids an easy attack to charge up Dominate so they can avoid consequences, then yeah - I'd be comfortable asking for a willpower.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your perspective. I'd appreciate fewer insults, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T16:27:28-07:00","id":947312,"title":"","content":"I think holy was talking about more specific weapons. So a club, yeah thats instinctual it basically follows the same motion as a swing. but a rapier? or a gun? both require a slight degree of thought to their use. <br /> <br /> Martial arts is as much mental as muscle memory, Both are a part of it but there is still a large degree of forethought to a fight. Ive heard a few martial artists describe their fights like a game of chess, once one makes a move the other counters and reacts. but yes a lot of it would become muscle memory.<br /> <br /> And looking for escape routes i would take to mean as you run. you dont plan your route. you just run. get as far away as possible from the thing youre running from. not plan out the best escape routes and short cuts. just run. <br /> <br /> But all of these examples leave a grey zone. How do you decide if the player is simply running, or running with a bit more of a plan in mind, or remembers enough of the area to plan a route? if you are stupid and mindless do you retain enough of your senses to use weapons properly?<br /> <br /> If you're arguing you cant speak because it isnt crazy mindless frenzy enough then it adds more questions.<br /> <br /> Are you even capable of defense in an anger frenzy? after all you lash out with over the top aggression, does that mean the player is forced to use the all out attack and get rid of their defense? Because deciding not to would certainly slow your chances of getting what you want. may be risky. but thats the beast? And that extends to physical intensity, do you have to spend your maximum blood each turn pumping your physical intensity because doing anything else would be slowing you sinking your teeth into that humans neck? <br /> <br /> Its just a little too grey of what can and cant be done in frenzy and just how far that extends with forcing you to use resources or the opposite end is just how in control you remain so that you can take actions like planning a dominate play to get someone alone and if not just where should the line be drawn. And it can be argued until the cows come home sadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:03:47-07:00","id":947363,"title":"","content":"Have you ever seen ( hopefully not in person) the terrified person keep swinging the baseball bat at the bad guy long after the bad guy has stopped twitching? Nothing but incoherent screams coming from the person while they swing? <br /> <br /> Or the person who unloads a full clip of bullets into the now unmoving threat while they continue to stand there and pull the trigger? <br /> <br /> The crazed psych can't get their target who went into the elevator, but takes all their rage out on the person who just got off instead.. <br /> <br /> More real: <br /> Has anyone scared you or startled you so badly all you can manage to do is scream or drop to the floor and laugh while you find words. <br /> <br /> Or you just swing and swing and then realize you just beat down your BFF? <br /> <br /> When you drop a Brick on your foot and all you can manage to do is swear. You can't even tell someone what happened because the only thing that comes to mind is &quot;fuck &quot; over and over. You can barely nod or shake your head to the onslaught of questions. <br /> <br /> People go into these &quot;frenzies&quot; all the time in movies or real life. Where they are too angry or too scared to speak or make rational logical choices. They simply react. <br /> <br /> Not sure why it's so hard to think of a vampire falling into that sort of state...<br /> <br /> As far as it being that way opening more questions. The answer is simple. How much blood that is spent is a player choice. Vampires are not aware that they have 13 vitae and can only spend 3 a turn or whatever. So spending any quantity on a physical discipline should suffice because your vampire doesn't know if it was 1 or 3 or 5. It was either a little or a lot. So that should answer how much gets spent per turn on physicals. <br /> <br /> The beast isn't suicidal. Maybe you go all out because you don't care at that moment what happens because all you want is to eat that person. If you were starving you wouldn't waste it...<br /> <br /> <br /> The one thing I think we will all agree on.. <br /> <br /> Do whatever works for your group. Whatever is best for you and your players, go with it. And that's perfectly acceptable. As long as you are having fun playing, that's what matters. If two players disagree, go with whatever the storyteller rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-09-2016, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}